      "writtenOn": "2024-03-18T22:22:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there further integration needed so these tools can find the `.build-id` directory?  Should `envsetup.sh` be setting an environment variable that points to it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "5e5f2105d4470102d33c2968454f25f669d8238b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "546e777b_469833a2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1067098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-18T23:39:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no existing environment variable that I am aware of that can specify these paths (at least llvm-symbolizer does not recognize any, and grepping for `/usr/lib/debug` in GNU binutils and LLDB did not reveal an existing one). Host tools such as the proposed `adb tombstone` will need to arrange to pass `--debug-file-directory $ANDROID_PRODUCT_OUT/symbols` to llvm-symbolizer.\n\nI was considering proposing the definition of an environment variable called `DEBUGPATH` which would be a colon-separated list of these paths. Once that is in place and llvm-symbolizer knows about it, we can start setting it and stop passing `--debug-file-directory` from the host tools. And if LLDB knows about it we could potentially simplify `gdbclient.py` by making it build-id based as well.",
      "parentUuid": "7005c3f8_605793ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 31
      },
